before:
The supplied HTML is separate from the CSS.

```html
<main><nav class="screen-tools">Page actions</nav><article><h1>Field report</h1><p>Water level stayed steady.</p><a href="https://example.org/report">Report source</a></article></main>
```

```css
body { font-family: serif; }
.screen-tools { padding: 12px; }
@media print { .screen-tools { display: none; } body { color: black; background: white; } a { color: black; text-decoration: underline; } }
```

Save this complete document as index.html, beside print.css containing the CSS above.

```html
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Field report</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="print.css"></head><body><main><nav class="screen-tools">Page actions</nav><article><h1>Field report</h1><p>Water level stayed steady.</p><a href="https://example.org/report">Report source</a></article></main></body></html>
```

after:
This rule hides the toolbar in print and gives the report dark text on a plain background.
```css
@media print {
  .screen-tools { display: none; }
  body { color: black; background: white; }
  a { color: black; text-decoration: underline; }
}
```
Outside print mode, these rules do not apply.
